+## UBU-D0341: Advisory sampling policy belongs to the operator's inference runtime
+
+**Status:** Accepted → DESIGN.md §1. Resolves `UBU-Q0185`; preserves `UBU-D0302`'s producer bounds and failure-attribution limits.
+
+For the MVP/Phase 2 advisory boundary, the operator configures sampling in the selected runtime. Add no generic decode Settings or UbU-selected temperature, top-p/top-k or repetition penalties, including hidden request overrides or automatic retry tuning. Preserve the existing model, endpoint, timeout and review seed/ceiling behavior; a review seed does not establish reproducibility across models or runtime versions.
+
+UbU still owns bounded validator-safe producer grammars, finite request/output and job budgets, cancellation, validation and ordinary candidate review/admission. Required grammar and resource/output-limit request fields remain within this boundary. An incompatible runtime leaves the affected operation unavailable with an explicit limitation and eligible retry/manual route. Abort, timeout and invalid output preserve saved state and cannot admit generated state changes, relax validation or authorize a new route. Retries retain current authority/input bindings and finite call/time budgets.
+
+Document adapter requirements and runtime configuration instructions. Record observable sampling configuration or its digest with qualified profiles, mark unknown effective defaults explicitly and repeat affected qualification checks after configuration changes where applicable under `UBU-D0331`/`UBU-D0336`. Require request-construction and failure-path fixtures before claiming conformance, as specified in DESIGN.md §1.
+
+This settles runtime-control ownership, not the cause of the already-bounded Vocabulary abort. The separate SuggestTags defect remains evidence for producer bounds, not a sampler diagnosis. No passing adapter fixtures, supported runtime configuration or implementation change is established by this decision.
